      "args": {
        "content": "# Requirements \u2014 Scaffolder Cross-Step Conditional Fields\n\n## In scope\n\n1. **Cross-step conditional field rendering in `Stepper` (`@backstage/plugin-scaffolder-react`)**: Support JSON Schema conditional constructs (`dependencies`, `if`/`then`/`else`, `allOf`, `oneOf`, `anyOf`) in a wizard step (`plugins/scaffolder-react/src/next/components/Stepper/**`, `plugins/scaffolder-react/src/next/hooks/**`, `plugins/scaffolder-react/src/next/lib/**`) that depend on parameter values answered in an earlier step of `Stepper`, so that conditional fields in a later step are shown or hidden based on earlier steps' answers in `stepsState`.\n2. **Per-step conditional validation in `Stepper` (`@backstage/plugin-scaffolder-react`)**: Enforce JSON Schema `required` and field validation rules on cross-step conditional fields only when the condition on the earlier step's answer is satisfied, without breaking per-step validation (`createAsyncValidators` and RJSF `validator`) or existing same-step conditional validation.\n3. **Back-navigation state cleanup and Review step filtering (`@backstage/plugin-scaffolder-react`)**: Ensure that navigating back (`handleBack` or step label click in `Stepper`) and changing an earlier step's answer updates form state and/or review resolution (`ReviewState` and `findSchemaForKey` in `plugins/scaffolder-react/src/next/components/ReviewState/**`) so fields whose cross-step or same-step conditions are no longer met are excluded from the Review step (`ReviewState`) and final `onCreate` submission payload.\n4. **Template wizard and template editor form preview compatibility (`@backstage/plugin-scaffolder`)**: Ensure `TemplateWizardPage` (`plugins/scaffolder/src/alpha/components/TemplateWizardPage/**`), `TemplateEditorForm` (`plugins/scaffolder/src/alpha/components/TemplateEditorPage/TemplateEditorForm*`), and `TemplateFormPreviewer` (`plugins/scaffolder/src/alpha/components/TemplateEditorPage/TemplateFormPreviewer*`) work seamlessly with cross-step conditional sc"
